s using SQL-based processing and ETL/ELT techniques, including incremental loads.<br>• Experience developing operational reports and dashboards in Power BI or Tableau; advanced Excel including pivot tables and formulas.<br>• Experience performing data validation, reconciliation, and troubleshooting data discrepancies.<br>• Strong understanding of data modeling and analytics dataset design (fact and dimension tables, star schemas).<br>• Ability to analyze large datasets and identify trends, patterns, and operational insights.<br>• Awareness of HIPAA and PHI handling, and strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills.<br><br>Preferred Knowledge/Skills *:<br>• Databricks Workflows, Unity Catalog, Auto Loader, and Databricks SQL dashboards.<br>• AWS Glue (jobs and Data Catalog), Athena, Lambda, and CloudWatch.<br>• Azure Data Factory and ADLS Gen2, since some engagements run on Azure.<br>• Experience building or supporting ETL/ELT pipelines, and migrating SQL Server logic to a lakehouse.<br>• Exposure to Alteryx, Informatica, or similar ETL tools.<br>• Git and basic CI/CD for data code.<br>• Microsoft Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate) for workflow automation.<br>• Experience with healthcare datasets or Revenue Cycle Management (RCM) environments, including EDI X12 835/837. Healthcare experience is not mandatory.<br><br>QUALIFICATIONS: Education / Experience:<br>• BE/BTECH, ME/MTECH, MBA, BCA/MCA, or a related field, or an equivalent amount of relevant professional experience.<br>• 4+ years of experience in data analytics, data engineering, or reporting roles.<br>• Hands-on experience with SQL databases and with Databricks (Spark SQL, Delta tables).<br>• Working experience with Python and with AWS data storage such as Amazon S3.<br>• Experience building dashboards, analytics datasets, and operational reports in Power BI or Tableau.<br>• Experience with ETL pipelines or data transformation workflows.<br>• Experience working with large operational datasets, including validation and reconciliation.<br>• Experience working in healthcare, insurance, or regulated industries is preferred.<br><br>Additional Information:<br>• Shift timings: Flexible to work in night shifts (US Time zone)<br>• Experience Level: 3–5 years<br>• Mode of working: Work from office<br>• Line of Service: Advisory<br>• Designation: Associate<br>• Role: Data Analyst (Databricks, SQL &amp; AWS)<br>• Location: Bangalore<br>• Primary Technology Stack: SQL Server, Databricks (Spark SQL, PySpark, Delta Lake), Python, AWS (S3, IAM), Power BI, Excel<br>• Preferred Technologies: Databricks Workflows / Unity Catalog / Auto Loader, AWS Glue / Athena / Lambda, Azure Data Factory, Tableau, Alteryx / Informatica, Git, Power Automate</span></div><div jsname="G7vtgf" class="TOQyFc Uzkg7d MmMIvd brKmxb" aria-controls="tsuid_lPH4auelCYuqhvcP5redoQQ_182" role="button" tabindex="0" jsaction="EMtXr" data-l="" data-hveid="CCgQQw" data-ved="2ahUKEwjnv8uh0YiYAxULleEIHeZbJ0QQl5ACegQIKBBD"><hr class="Bi9oQd" aria-hidden="true"><div class="Wjtive btku5b rXoM2c sjVJQd"><div class="niO4u VDgVie SlP8xc"><span class="cHaqb"><span class="PBBEhf">Show full description</span></span><span class="T2xY9b w2fKdd z1asCe" aria-hidden="true" style="height:18px;line-height:18px;width:18px"><svg focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960"><path d="M480-344L240-584l56-56L480-456L664-640l56,56L480-344Z"></path></svg></span></div></div></div></div></div><div class="XFOJCe" data-ved="2ahUKEwjnv8uh0YiYAxULleEIHeZbJ0QQ5ZkFegQIKBBE"><div class="EyBRub" data-ved="2ahUKEwjnv8uh0YiYAxULleEIHeZbJ0QQyo8CegQIKBBF"><div jscontroller="Wo3n8" jsname="aadvhe" jsmodel=" d5EhJe" data-bkt="horizon_jobs" data-fhs="" data-maindata='[null,null,"bind(&#39;java/com/google/gws/plugins/horizon/jobs/viewer/herocontent/jslayout/feedback_messages.html#JobAtEmployer&#39;,{employer_name:&#39;PwC&#39;,job_title:&#39;Data Analyst-Associate&#39;})","_lPH4auelCYuqhvcP5redoQ