dv1_Ac3VAox2vYm1atAXXoNEGodQcZIRDQGMuVtys1e89_YEqkImbA\u0026source\u003dsh/x/job/li/m1/1#fpstate\u003dtldetail\u0026htivrt\u003djobs\u0026htiq\u003dData+Analyst+in+Bengaluru+with+5+years+of+experience+jobs\u0026htidocid\u003dbeD8dqkvG_RoudVOAAAAAA%3D%3D",null,null,"Data Management Analyst",null,null,null,null,1,null,37,["H4sIAAAAAAAA_xXOMQrCQBBAUWxzBBunE0R2g2CjlSJYSM4QJnHYRDczYWcCSecRBG_oSYzN7x787L3I8gsaQoGMgTpigxNjnNTg-_rAQypQwlQ3IAxXkRBpeWzMej14rxpdUENra1dL54WpktHPSP8ptcFEfUSjcrfPR9dz2KwKkfu0VmgZzsQB45CGLdww8fzxxB-54M-FkwAAAA","v1_Ac3VAox2vYm1atAXXoNEGodQcZIRDQGMuVtys1e89_YEqkImbA"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,0]],"lPH4auelCYuqhvcP5redoQQ51":[[0,"https://careers.moodys.com/en/job/bengaluru/data-management-analyst/49841/100021822352","jobs","9BsvqXb84G1MIM","\u003cp\u003eAt Moody's, we unite the brightest minds to turn today’s risks into tomorrow’s opportunities. We do this by striving to create an inclusive environment where everyone feels welcome to be who they are—with the freedom to exchange ideas, think innovatively, and listen to each other and customers in meaningful ways. Moody’s is transforming how the world sees risk. As a global leader in ratings and integrated risk assessment, we’re advancing AI to move from insight to action—enabling intelligence that not only understands complexity but responds to it. We decode risk to unlock opportunity, helping our clients navigate uncertainty with clarity, speed, and confidence.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are excited about this opportunity but do not meet every single requirement, please apply! You still may be a great fit for this role or other open roles. We are seeking candidates who model our values: invest in every relationship, lead with curiosity, champion diverse perspectives, turn inputs into actions, and uphold trust through integrity. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSkills and Competencies\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e2 to 5 years of experience in data management, data quality, data governance, or related analytical functions\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eStrong knowledge of structured finance products, including Residential Mortgage-Backed Securities, Asset-Backed Securities, Commercial Mortgage-Backed Securities, and Collateralized Loan Obligations\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience working with data acquisition, validation, enrichment, cleansing, and Master Data Management initiatives\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAdvanced SQL skills with the ability to analyze, transform, and manage large datasets\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eStrong analytical and problem-solving skills, including root cause analysis and process improvement\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExcellent communication and collaboration skills with the ability to work effectively across global and cross-functional teams\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience with Python, VBA, automation, or scripting tools is preferred\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eKnowledge of project management practices and software development lifecycle methodologies is preferred\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEducation\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eBachelor's degree in Business, Finance, Economics, Data Management, Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field required/ MBA or equivalent graduate degree preferred\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eResponsibilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eSupport the acquisition, management, governance, and quality of structured finance data to enable downstream products, analytics, and business growth\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eManage the end-to-end production lifecycle for structured finance datasets, including agency and non-agency residential mortgage-backed securities, asset-backed securities, commercial mortgage-backed securities, and collateralized debt obligations\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAcquire, validate, transform, and maintain data to support analytics products and operational processes.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eMonitor data quality, investigate discrepancies, and implement corrective actions to ensure data accuracy, consistency, and completeness\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCoordinate vendor operations by managing submissions, resolving inquiries, defining requirements, establishing acceptance criteria, and approving deliverables\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePartner with Data Operations and Development teams to prioritize requirements, create and track work items, and support production activities\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eEstablish and maintain structured asset data governance processes, standards, and controls\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLead initiatives focused on data cleansing, enrichment, and process optimization to improve operational efficiency and data integrity\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eContribute to enterprise-wide data quality and Master Data Management initiatives\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eEvaluate and recommend new technologies, tools, and best practices that enhance data management capabilities\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSupport cross-functional stakeholders through analysis, reporting, and continuous improvement efforts\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbout the Team\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur Content Solutions - Structured Finance team is responsible for acquiring, managing, and delivering high-quality structured finance data that powers Moody's analytics solutions and client offerings\u003cbr\u003eBy joining our team, you will:\u003cbr\u003eHelp drive the quality, accuracy, and coverage of structured finance datasets used across Moody's products\u003cbr\u003eCollaborate with global teams across data operations, technology, and product functions\u003cbr\u003eContribute to innovative data management and governance initiatives 